  "_notes": "Keyed by Kodi core id. Files are relative to the Kodi/libretro system directory; when every file of a core lives in one subdirectory it is given as 'subdir' and the names are bare, otherwise names carry their relative path (bluemsx). Derived from Grout bios/data/core_requirements.json where the core exists there (mednafen_psx_hw -> beetle-psx, mednafen_* -> beetle-*, mupen64plus_next -> mupen64plus-nx, puae -> uae, puae2021 -> uae2021, bsnes -> beetle-bsnes and bsnes, genesis_plus_gx -> genplus, underscores -> dashes), snes9x2010 from its source, otherwise from the BIOS section of docs.libretro.com/library/<core>/. Known discrepancies kept as Grout has them: o2em lists all four Videopac ROMs as required although the core only loads o2rom.bin; yabasanshiro marks saturn_bios.bin required while libretro docs say optional; dolphin's codehandler.bin is the Sys file Grout tracks, the optional GC IPL.bin lives under saves, not system.",
